      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have tested the changes in version 2025.4.2p1.\n\nFrom what I’ve checked, the stereo separation for audio sources at very close range has definitely improved.\n\nPreviously, it felt like the spatial audio originated directly from the Viewpoint. Now, it feels like the audio origin has shifted slightly behind the Viewpoint (closer to the avatar's actual ears). While I don't know the exact internal mechanics, this results in a much more natural sound field for most humanoid avatars.\n\nThis has significantly increased immersion, especially for ASMR content. Thank you for the fix!\n\nRegarding the changes to volume levels and directivity, I believe these are things we can simply adapt to over time.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
